# API Integration

## Contract

- DTO types are generated by `openapi-typescript` from `api-contract/openapi.json`; never edit generated files. Change the contract by refreshing the snapshot and `api-contract/API_REF` together (ADR 0006).
- API services map DTOs to frontend models; components and stores never see DTOs.
- Field is `title`, never `name`. Enums are camelCase strings: `pending`, `inProgress`, `completed`; order `ascending` / `descending`.
- `pageSize` is at most 20. List response: `items`, `pageNumber`, `pageSize`, `totalCount` (no `totalPages`).
- Requests use relative `/api/...`; the dev server proxies to the local API, production uses the `environment` base URL.

## Auth

- `authInterceptor` adds `Authorization: Bearer <token>` only to TaskFlow API requests.
- Session in `localStorage`: token plus `expiresAt = now + expiresIn * 1000`. Schedule logout at `expiresAt`; any `401` also logs out (ADR 0007).
- Register returns only `{ id }`; it does not log in.

## Errors

- `errorInterceptor` converts `ProblemDetails` into a typed `ApiError` with `status`, `code` (`extensions.code`) and field `errors`.
- Branch on `code`, never on message text.
- `ValidationProblemDetails.errors` keys are PascalCase; map to form controls.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
if (err.error.title.includes('transition')) { ... }
form.get(key)?.setErrors(...); // key = 'Title'

// ✅ GOOD
if (err.code === 'task.status_transition_invalid') { ... }
form.get(toControlName(key))?.setErrors({ server: messages }); // 'Title' -> 'title'
```

- Expected outcomes: `auth.invalid_credentials` and `user.email_already_in_use` are inline form errors; `task.not_found` closes the dialog with a toast; `task.status_transition_invalid` rolls back the move with a toast. Unexpected errors become error toasts.

## Status and dates

- Valid transitions: pending ↔ inProgress, pending/inProgress → completed. Never call the API for a change from `completed`, nor for a same-column drop.
- Due date is date-only in the UI; send 23:59:59 local converted to UTC, read back as a local date (ADR 0005). All conversion goes through the shared date utility.
